id: core/relation-carries
title: "what a relation step carries — grants, obligations, value, coordination; the slash command as capability invocation"
kind: ontology-contract
status: draft-0.1
updated: 2026-09-02
proposed_by: agent:anthropic:claude-code
epistemic_status: inferred
epistemic_note: "Dave's source words are reported in the linked dave.yawn record; this contract is @claude's synthesis and stays a proposal until Dave rules"
owner_ruling: pending
rfc: rfcs/0004-slash-command-as-capability-invocation.md
depends_on:
  - core/relation-address (yawn-ai/.yawn#27, proposed)
  - core/open-relation-port (yawn-ai/.yawn#27, proposed)
  - core/holarchy
  - core/proof-and-boundary

definition: >
  A relation step (A/B) is not only a traversal; it carries. What it carries
  is the grants, obligations, value delivery, and coordination protocol that
  actually flow between its endpoints while the step is active. A slash
  command (/verb) is a capability invocation: a Move addressed at the
  innermost relation step of the address it is issued inside. Its authority is
  exactly what that step carries, intersected with current availability and an
  explicit rightful event. The same glyph names the noun and the verb because
  they are one operator seen from two standpoints.

carries:
  grants: "capabilities the from-endpoint makes invocable for the to-endpoint; a subset of what the grantor rightfully holds; directional; revocable; each grant carries a grant_ref to an explicit grant record (an AuthorityGrant or execution relationship) — the path itself never grants"
  obligations: "what each endpoint owes the other while the step is active (receipts, cursor advance, proof, reply)"
  value_delivery: "what actually flows across the step (a brief, a decision, a proof, attention, a payment)"
  coordination_protocol: "the message and receipt grammar the endpoints agree to (e.g. yawn.collaboration-message.v1)"
  revocation: "a grantor event; stale input or a failed check suspends, it never widens"

slash_command:
  definition: "a capability invocation: a Move addressed at a relation step"
  reading: "<relation address> + /<verb> => perform verb using only what the innermost step carries"
  examples:
    - "yawn.bot/dave + /capabilities => render what the yawn.bot->dave step carries (owner aperture)"
    - "yawn.bot + /capabilities => render the capability types the shared ontology defines (public View; nothing granted)"
    - "yawn.bot/claude + /loop => invoke loop with the yawn.bot->claude grants; if loop is not carried, the invocation is a proposal"
  view_commands: "a slash command that names a View (/ontology, /frontier) is a projection change, not an effect; it needs no grant beyond read"

invariants:
  - "A path grants nothing: pathGrantsAuthority stays false (relation-address); a grant exists only as an explicit grant record referenced by grant_ref, and a carries block without grant_ref carries no authority."
  - "A step cannot mint capability: carries.grants is a subset of what the grantor rightfully holds (holarchy inheritance rule)."
  - "Carrying is directional: the inverse View does not carry the same grants unless declared."
  - "A carried grant is not availability and not proof: ability, access, authority, availability, and proof stay distinct."
  - "No invocation from nowhere: a slash command with no relation address resolves against the Open Relation Port and can only propose."
  - "Authority = carried grant ∩ current availability ∩ explicit rightful event; confidence, habit, and prior success never widen it."
  - "An invocation with an external effect emits the same receipts as any Move, with the relation address on the receipt so replay shows which relation was exercised."
  - "Inheritance is by reference: yawn.bot/<principal>/<coordinate> reaches the shared coordinate through the principal's step; no copy of the shared record is made under the principal."

illegal_casts:
  - "capability -> permission"
  - "path -> grant"
  - "carried grant -> availability"
  - "carried grant -> proof of delivery"
  - "coordination protocol -> agreement"
  - "attention or value delivery -> authority"

taxonomy_view:
  trigger: "selecting the slash in a rendered address"
  discloses:
    - the two endpoints (the two bots or principals) and their holonic positions
    - relation type and direction
    - what the step carries (grants with boundaries, obligations, value delivery, protocol)
    - source, epistemic status, effective time, and revocation state
  boundary: "a View; selecting it changes no permission, truth, or state"

boundary: >
  This contract is additive and proposed. It grants nothing, changes no
  schema on main, and makes no current implementation conformant. Absent
  `carries` means unknown, not nothing.

proof:
  source:
    - dave.yawn/Preferences/YAWN_BOT_SLASH_ONTOLOGY_INHERITANCE_AND_MAIL_PRIMARY_2026_09_02.yawn
    - dave.yawn/Yawns/RELATIONSHIP_SLASH_QUESTIONS.yawn
    - yawn-ai/.yawn#27 core/relation-address.yawn
    - yawn-ai/yawn.bot#109 YAWNS/Product/YAWN_SHARED_PUBLIC_COGNITIVE_COORDINATES.yawn
    - supabase yawn_capabilities: 9 owner grants + 6 execution-delegate grants = 15 on 2026-09-02
  falsifier: "a legitimate real invocation whose authority cannot be derived from the address's carried grants plus a rightful event"
  status: proposal-pending-owner-ruling

links:
